pseudo-Boolean proof version 3.0
% refused-at: parse
% INTEGRATION-TEST: lenient-header-counts
% Regression test: `Lit` packs `(var_idx << 1) ^ is_negated` into a `usize`, so
% the DIMACS literal -9223372036854775807 has the packed value `usize::MAX` --
% which is exactly the `Lit::new_undef()` value that `from_unnormalized_lits`
% used as its "no previous literal" sentinel. The literal was read as a
% duplicate of nothing and dropped, so this unit clause was stored as the empty
% clause, i.e. a contradiction, and `rup >= 1` verified UNSAT for a formula
% that is satisfiable (x1 true, the second variable false). The CNF parser is
% the only place a variable index comes from untrusted text, and the range
% check there is unconditional -- `--lenient-header-counts` must not turn it
% off, which is why this instance carries that flag and must still be rejected.
f 2;
rup >= 1;
output NONE;
conclusion UNSAT : 3;
end pseudo-Boolean proof;
